# Record-from-the-editor QA (just qa-editor Tests/QA/record.qa): F10 / Run > Play and Record, start to saved dialog.
# End to end, for a person (or the controller) with a display and ffmpeg on PATH; NOT run in CI. The Demo project opens
# from the command line (the recipe builds it first). `wait` counts frames. No verb waits for the recording to be
# saved, so a fixed wait covers the finalise (the pad and mux of a few seconds of footage); lengthen it on a slow disk.
# Review the PNGs in artifacts/qa-editor: the toolbar shows "● REC m:ss" while recording, then the Recording saved dialog.
wait 30
wait-for project 300
capture 01-ready
# 1. Nothing runs: Play and Record launches the main scene with --record, so the file covers the game from its first frame.
command play.record
wait-for playing 180
wait 60
capture 02-recording
wait 180
# F10 again stops: the toolbar says "Saving recording…", then the game reports the file.
command play.record
wait 30
capture 03-saving
wait 600
capture 04-saved-dialog
cancel
wait 10
command play.stop
wait-for stopped 30
wait 30
# 2. Mid-session: a plain Play (F5), then record while it runs (the editor passed --frame-capture at launch).
command play.main
wait-for playing 180
wait 60
command play.record
wait 120
capture 05-recording-midsession
command play.record
wait 600
capture 06-saved-dialog-midsession
cancel
wait 10
command play.stop
wait-for stopped 30
wait 30
quit
